@startuml task-lifecycle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
title Task order → Accepted → report → collection (0.22.1)
actor Owner
participant "Chat / MCP client" as Chat
participant "MCP server" as MCP
collections "Queue / durable requests" as Queue
participant "Watch" as Watch
participant "Git / setup" as Git
participant "tmux / provider" as Agent
database "State / journal / report" as State
Owner -> Chat: Request a concrete task
Chat -> MCP: events_since(as: chat:name)
MCP --> Chat: Changes since this client's cursor
Chat -> MCP: new / queue(spec) — preview
MCP --> Chat: Plan + preview_token + expiry
Chat -> Owner: Show task IDs, repos, branch/base, model/effort, after, cost
Owner --> Chat: Confirm this plan
Chat -> MCP: confirm: true, preview_token (same session)
MCP -> Queue: Persist accepted spec under short accept lock
MCP --> Chat: Accepted (registration; not started/completed)
Watch -> Queue: Next tick: validate accepted spec
alt invalid spec / changed facts
 Watch -> Queue: failed + reason
 Watch -> State: Start failure event + notification
else valid and eligible
 Watch -> Git: Worktree → per-repo setup → links
 Watch -> Agent: Start interactive provider window
 alt folder trust / first-run dialog
  Agent --> Owner: needs-trust / needs-input
  Owner -> Agent: Answer in task window
 end
 Watch -> Agent: Wait for structural ready input; paste prompt
 Agent --> Watch: Delivery acknowledgement / turn start
 Watch -> State: Delivery confirmed / start event
 group Work and follow-ups
  Agent -> Git: Work in assigned checkout
  alt needs-input menu
   Watch -> State: Question event
   Chat -> MCP: events_since → peek
   Owner -> Chat: Select answer
   Chat -> MCP: answer(task, option, token), preview → confirm
   MCP -> Agent: Safe answer (explicit owner-approved menu only)
  else send while Codex is busy
   Chat -> MCP: send(task, text), preview → confirm
   MCP -> Queue: Accepted send request (with watcher)
   Watch -> State: queued_until_turn_end + message_id
   Agent --> Watch: Confirmed idle / turn end
   Watch -> Agent: Deliver durable queued follow-up
  else limited
   Watch -> State: limited event
   Owner -> MCP: send continuation / move — preview → confirm
   MCP -> Agent: Continue live window / mapped provider in same worktree
  note right of Agent: resume recreates a missing window after loss.
  else cancel
   Owner -> MCP: cancel — preview → confirm
   MCP -> Queue: Accepted request (with watcher)
   Watch -> Agent: Interrupt then close window
   Watch -> State: cancelled; worktree and branch retained
  end
 end
 Agent -> State: Verdict first line + attempt marker + outputs + report-end
 Watch -> State: Current report complete / report-ready event
 Chat -> MCP: events_since(as: chat:name)
 MCP --> Chat: Report verdict + current summary
 Chat -> MCP: get_report(task), contiguous pages to EOF
 MCP --> Chat: Full report; mark pulled only after full delivery
 Owner -> Chat: Review and approve closure
 Chat -> MCP: close — preview → confirm
 MCP -> Queue: Accepted close request (with watcher)
 Watch -> Agent: Close window; optional protected worktree removal
end
== Other durable paths ==
group failed start → queue_retry
 Watch -> Agent: Input never becomes ready
 Watch -> State: Save start-failure-screen.txt; queue failed
 note right of Agent: Keep diagnostic window by default\n(start_failure.keep_window)
 Owner -> MCP: queue_retry — preview → confirm
 MCP -> Queue: Accepted retry
 Watch -> Agent: Close leftover failed window; retry validation/start
end
group after + BLOCKED
 Watch -> State: Read predecessor's first-line verdict
 alt rejected verdict (FAIL / BLOCKED / NO-GO by default)
  Watch -> Queue: Block dependent; notify
  Owner -> MCP: unblock(task, drop_after?) — preview → confirm
  MCP -> Queue: Accepted dependency change
  Watch -> Queue: Apply; re-evaluate eligibility
 else report incomplete / author still active
  Watch -> Queue: Wait for verdict
 else corrected report now accepted
  Watch -> Queue: Auto-unblock at next tick; emit unblocked
 end
end
group watch restarts mid-task
 Watch -> State: Reload durable tasks, queue, pending delivery
 Watch -> Agent: Reconcile live windows; continue monitoring
 note right of Watch: Live windows survive watch restart.\nLost metadata: explicit adopt.\nLost windows: explicit resume, no duplicate initial prompt.
end
@enduml
